# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirects

# Domain-wide redirect from old domain to new domain
https://wecreatethis.pages.dev/* https://wecreatethis.com/:splat 301

# Client-side routing support for sub-apps

# Every other top-level app folder (session 027: these silently stopped
# resolving once the blog homepage move added the final /* /section 200
# catch-all - the wildcard always wins over a real static file/folder per
# Cloudflare Pages docs, "redirects are always followed regardless of
# whether an asset matches the incoming request" - so every app needs an
# explicit pass-through here or it renders the blog shell instead of itself.
# Rule targets use :splat, not a literal /app/index.html - Cloudflare's
# build-time loop detector silently drops any rule whose destination would
# re-normalize back to match its own source pattern (e.g. /app/index.html
# stripping back down to /app/), and does so with no runtime error, just a
# build-log warning nobody sees. Two lines per app: the bare path (no
# trailing slash) redirects to the trailing-slash form, since a lone
# /app/* splat requires something after the slash to match.
/invisibleink  /invisibleink/  301
/invisibleink/*  /invisibleink/:splat  200
/tarot  /tarot/  301
/tarot/*  /tarot/:splat  200
/birdle  /birdle/  301
/birdle/*  /birdle/:splat  200
